# Demo UI — Test Coverage Required

When editing demo **test-related logic** (scenario flows, log classification, narrative prompts, E2E assertion helpers), add or update the matching unit tests in the **same session**.

## Change → test map

| Change | Required test file |
|---|---|
| Log classification, hints, baseline, step overrides | [`tests/observability-log-rules.spec.ts`](../../tests/observability-log-rules.spec.ts) |
| Scenario hops, flows, responses, overlays, prompts | [`tests/demo-scenario-consistency.spec.ts`](../../tests/demo-scenario-consistency.spec.ts) |
| E2E assertion patterns (`hasCredentialProbeEvidence`, network/guardrails checks) | [`tests/ui-helpers.unit.spec.ts`](../../tests/ui-helpers.unit.spec.ts) |
| Presentation HTML/JS styling | [`scripts/validate-demo-external-css.sh`](../../scripts/validate-demo-external-css.sh) — see [`demo-external-css.mdc`](./demo-external-css.mdc) |
| New demo scenario (E, F, …) | Extend `demo-prompts.ts`, `narrative-data.js`, `overall-flows.js` **and** all three specs above |

## Source files under test

| Module | Spec |
|---|---|
| `docs/demo/v1/observability-log-rules.js` | `observability-log-rules.spec.ts` |
| `docs/demo/scenarios/overall-flows.js`, `overall-response-maps.js`, `scenario-responses.js` | `demo-scenario-consistency.spec.ts` |
| `docs/demo/v1/narrative-data.js` + `tests/demo-prompts.ts` | `demo-scenario-consistency.spec.ts` |
| `tests/ui-helpers.ts` | `ui-helpers.unit.spec.ts` |

Pure layout constants live in `docs/demo/scenarios/scenario-layout.js` (no FlowStory/DOM) so scenario modules remain importable in Node unit tests.

## Gate before done

From repo root:

```bash
./scripts/validate-demo-ui.sh
```

Exit code `0` = pass. Non-zero = fix tests or implementation, then re-run.

## Do not

- Add classification rules or scenario hops without a failing-then-passing fixture
- Rely on cluster E2E (`demo-narrative.spec.ts`) as the only guard for presenter data
- Skip tests when only “renaming” hop labels if message content or step order changes

## Workflow

For refactor or audit workflows, use the **`demo-ui-tests`** skill.
